theory.intro:
A **sector** is the region between two radii and the arc joining them. Its area is the fraction $\dfrac{\theta}{2\pi}$ of the circle area $\pi r^{2}$, which simplifies to $A = \tfrac{1}{2}r^{2}\theta$. Convert degrees to radians first.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (3,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (-1.5,2.598);
\fill[gray!35] (O) -- (P) arc (0:120:3) -- cycle;
\draw (O) circle (3);
\draw[thick] (O) -- (P) node[midway, below] {$r$};
\draw[thick] (O) -- (Q) node[midway, above left] {$r$};
\draw[thick] (P) arc (0:120:3);
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=P--O--Q};
\node at (60:2.1) {$A$};
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
A minor sector of angle $90^{\circ}$ is removed from a circle of radius $8\text{ cm}$. Find the exact area of the remaining major sector.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) circle (2);
\draw (0,2)--(0,0)--(2,0);
\draw (0.35,0)--(0.35,0.35)--(0,0.35);
\path (1,-0.3) node {$8\text{ cm}$};
\path (0.9,0.8) node {$90^{\circ}$};
\path (-0.7,-0.9) node {Remaining region};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A wiper sweeps the region between concentric arcs of radii $12\text{ cm}$ and $24\text{ cm}$ through an angle of $120^{\circ}$. Find the exact area swept.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (2.4,0) arc (0:120:2.4)--(120:1.2) arc (120:0:1.2)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(1.2,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(120:1.2);
\draw (0.5,0) arc (0:120:0.5);
\path (60:0.85) node {$120^{\circ}$};
\path (0.65,-0.3) node {$12\text{ cm}$};
\draw[<->] (0,-0.7)--(2.4,-0.7);
\path (1.2,-1) node {$24\text{ cm}$};
\path (-0.2,-0.2) node {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

